-- title:
--   Base mass of a one-point divisor
-- statement:
--   Fix $N \ge 1$ and let $\overline{F}_N =$ `modularFunctionFieldBar N` be the intermediate field of $\mathrm{LaurentSeries}(\overline{\mathbb{Q}})$ over $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ generated by the coefficientwise image of the modular function field `modularFunctionFieldFull N`. Let $r$ be a natural number and $s : \mathrm{Fin}\,r \to \overline{F}_N$ a finite family of elements of this field. Let $v$ be a place of $\overline{F}_N$ over $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$, i.e. a valuation subring of $\overline{F}_N$ containing $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$, different from the whole field and a principal ideal ring, and assume $v \ne$ `cuspInftyBar N`, the $q$-adic place at the cusp at infinity. Then for every integer $n$, the divisor $n \cdot v$, i.e. the finitely supported function `Finsupp.single v n` on places, satisfies
--   $$\mathrm{baseMass}_N^{\,s}(n\cdot v) \;=\; n \cdot \mathrm{baseHt}_s(\text{cusp}, v),$$
--   where $\mathrm{baseMass}_N^{\,s}(D)$ is by definition the sum of $D_w \cdot \mathrm{baseHt}_s(\text{cusp}, w)$ over the support of $D$ with the cusp erased, and $\mathrm{baseHt}_s(\text{cusp}, w)$ is $0$ when $w$ is the cusp and otherwise equals $\mathrm{pairHt}_s(w, \text{cusp}) = \mathrm{pointHt}_s(w) + \mathrm{pointHt}_s(\text{cusp}) - \mathrm{absLogHeight}(\mathrm{chordVec}\,s\,w\,\text{cusp})$.
--
--   This is the evaluation of the base mass, a linear functional on divisors of the modular curve that weights each non-cuspidal place by its base height relative to the cusp at infinity, on a divisor supported at a single non-cuspidal place. It is used to track the base mass along the operations on divisor representatives of classes in $J_0(N)$, in [`ModularCurve.JZero.exists_isRepOf_baseMass_le_heightForm`](thm.html#ModularCurve.JZero.exists_isRepOf_baseMass_le_heightForm) and in [`ModularCurve.JZero.heightForm_eq_genusFF_mul_baseMass_of_offBaseMass_le_one`](thm.html#ModularCurve.JZero.heightForm_eq_genusFF_mul_baseMass_of_offBaseMass_le_one).
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_ModularCurve_JZero_baseMass_single.lean

